      "usage": "× she that was with child, fill(-ed, -ed with), full(-ly), multitude, as is worth.",
      "full": "H4392. male מָלֵא adjective full ; — ׳מ Gen 23:9 15 t.; construct מְלֵא Jer 6:11 ; feminine מְלֵאָה Num 7:14 20 t.; construct מְלֵאֲתִי Isa 1:21 compare Ges § 90 . 3 a.; plural מְלֵאִים Num 7:13 18 t.; feminine מְלֵאוֺת ( אֹת -) Gen 41:7 4 t.; — full , absolute of ears of corn 41:7 , 22 ; of value, price, 23:9 ; 1Chr 21:22 , 24 ; of wind (= strong) Jer 4:12 followed by accusative of material, bowls of fine flour ( סֹלֶת ) Num 7:13 , 19 , 25 , 31 , 37 , 43 , 49 , 55 , 61 , 67 , 73, 79; spoons of incense 7:14 ; 7:20 ; 7:26 ; 7:32 ; 7:38 ; 7:44 ; 7:50 ; 7:56 ; 7:62 ; 7:68 ; 7:74 ; 7:80 ; 7:86 ; bowls of wine Jer 35:5 , compare figurative Psa 75:9 ; houses, of contents Deut 6:11 ; Neh 9:25 compare Prov 17:1 ; cage, of birds Jer 5:27 (in simile, see below); cart, of sheaves Amos 2:13 (in simile) 1Chr 11:13 ; 2Kin 7:15 ; Ezek 1:18 ; 10:12 ; 17:3 ; 36:38 ; 37:1 ; as predicate, of storehouses Psa 144:13 ; compare figurative of Naomi Ruth 1:21 ; of sea Eccl 1:7 ; with article, of full vessel 2Kin 4:4 ; מְלֵאָה pregnant woman Eccl 11:5 ; figurative full of blessing Deut 33:23 ; wisdom 34:9 ; justice Isa 1:21 ; commotion 22:2 ; fury 51:20 ; lies, etc. Nahum 3:1 ; wisdom Ezek 28:12 (strike out A B Co); only twice in construct before that with which a thing is filled Isa 1:21 ׳מ מִשְׁמָּט ; Jer 6:11 יָמִים מְלֵא (as substantive); as substantive in Genitive (Ges § 128n ) Psa 73:10 מָלֵא מֵי ; as adverb = fully Nahum 1:10 ; Jer 12:6 (loudly, compare 4:5 ).",
